{"base_rate":0.2943495400788436,"brier":0.1255520367936925,"bss":0.39553553887337056,"bss_hi":0.5018661079650308,"bss_lo":0.2619410102056391,"chart":{"base":[443.7,55.4],"fp":[176.5,265.6],"lead":"62,257.2 272,234.1 482,196.1 692,138.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.40 — higher than 72% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 59% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 1%; promised 92% → rained 69%"},"rel":"78.7,461.7 293.4,432.1 643.4,169"},"country":"JP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16216819973718793,"ess":417.8901734104047,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Kyoto</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Kyoto rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.40, ranked 59 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(19&ndash;120) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>220</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>236</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Kyoto</b> <span class=\"muted\">Japan</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.40</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>19&ndash;120\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Kyoto &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Kyoto\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.11027272727273,377.03636363636366 89.05928571428572,330.0 147.86542857142854,252.0 221.86361445783135,171.49397590361446 312.93205882352936,82.23529411764707 405.355,19.542372881355902 405.355,31.881355932203405 312.93205882352936,157.17647058823528 221.86361445783135,254.8192771084337 147.86542857142854,324.8 89.05928571428572,369.0 59.11027272727273,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"274.8567674113009\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"274.8567674113009\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.11027272727273,378.6909090909091 89.05928571428572,377.6666666666667 147.86542857142854,366.4 221.86361445783135,342.5301204819277 312.93205882352936,301.70588235294116 405.355,82.77966101694915\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 220 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"59.11027272727273\" cy=\"378.6909090909091\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"89.05928571428572\" cy=\"377.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"147.86542857142854\" cy=\"366.4\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"221.86361445783135\" cy=\"342.5301204819277\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 72%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"312.93205882352936\" cy=\"301.70588235294116\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 236 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"405.355\" cy=\"82.77966101694915\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(29%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Kyoto the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.63) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.16).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>0.161</td><td class='num'>17.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.239</td><td class='num'>19.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.332</td><td class='num'>19.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.634</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.02107,"lon":135.75385,"n":761,"n_cities":213,"name":"Kyoto","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003136363636363637,"n":220,"obs":0.00909090909090909,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.08773809523809525,"n":84,"obs":0.011904761904761904,"sig":true},{"hi":0.33,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.2538571428571428,"n":70,"obs":0.04285714285714286,"sig":true},{"